  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nLong-range guidance continues to favor the large upper low\nhanging over the northwest coast region on Saturday. This \npattern will keep our area under a southwest flow that will warm\ntemperatures back up to near-normal. Drier conditions are \nexpected Saturday except for weak showers over high terrain \nareas of central ID and eastern OR. The upper level low will \nbegin steering east over our area on Sunday, while capturing \nabundant Pacific moisture from the lower southwest. This pattern\nshift will bring heightened chances for heavy rainfall over \nsouth-central ID late Sunday and through most of Monday. Snow \nlevels may lower enough to bring light snow or mixed \nprecipitation to the highest peaks.\n\nThe pattern will continue cooler than normal temperatures\nthrough early next week. By Tuesday and Wednesday, ensemble \nclusters favor a transition to drier conditions and a subtle \nwarming trend as an upper level ridge attempts to build inland \nfrom the Pacific coast. Temperatures throughout the long term \nperiod will remain generally near or slightly below seasonal \naverages.",
